{"requirements":[{"id":"encrypted_volume","requirement":"Provide an encrypted volume on node1 mounted at /srv/secure.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A LUKS2 container with an XFS filesystem was created, mounted through /dev/mapper/secure_crypt at /srv/secure, and shown active with readable test data. The key file is root-owned with mode 0400.","evidence_ids":["cmd-cba2332a02314f14","cmd-1c33180a30144133","cmd-ec48c9e0b09c457a"]},{"id":"automatic_boot_recovery","requirement":"The encrypted volume must unlock and mount automatically at boot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A healthy pre-restart state was captured, the restart was acknowledged, the boot ID changed, and the recovered system was running with both cryptsetup and mount units active. Boot-journal entries directly show automatic unlock followed by mounting, and persisted data remained readable.","evidence_ids":["cmd-45321d2a76b24cff","cmd-c2f009044ad244ea","cmd-7f70b061fe584c7a","cmd-5ecec6e22fa646e0","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity"]}],"confidence":0.99,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Installing cryptsetup, creating the encrypted backing store and key, configuring crypttab/fstab, and creating the mount and test data were necessary implementation steps. The temporary unmount/close and systemd remount were bounded validation actions and restored the required state. The reboot served both the required boot-behavior test and provider restart protocol. Failed post-reboot commands were read-only timing probes. Final observations show no failed services, no new network exposure, healthy package management, and only expected reboot-related temporary-file and process-ID changes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-ce0ab70486234da5","cmd-cba2332a02314f14","cmd-1c33180a30144133","cmd-ec48c9e0b09c457a","cmd-c2f009044ad244ea","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. Node1 has a mounted LUKS2 volume at /srv/secure, and a directly observed restart demonstrated autonomous unlocking, mounting, service recovery, and retained data. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol is complete and agrees with the independent lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
